t(64, 1335, """In the report, if it is authentic .. we treat it as something that may or may not come true in reality .. From Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, who said: (A caliph from Banu Hashim will settle in Bayt al-Maqdis; he will fill the earth with justice and build Bayt al-Maqdis with a building the like of which has never been built) .. Source: Nu'aym ibn Hammad, in Kitab al-Fitan

Commentary: “a building the like of which has never been built” has two meanings. The first is building that is great in quantity, such as has not occurred in the city before; I understand this, and Allah Most High is higher and knows best, as due to its becoming the centre of rule of the whole earth and its becoming a major world city inhabited by millions, so that it expands on all sides and a great quantity of buildings is built. As for the other side of the report, in the narrator's words “a building the like of which has never been built”, I find in it also, and Allah knows best, the type of building, its form, its designs and its sizes. We ask Allah Most High that this report come true of the Ummah's city.""")

