t(74, 725, """100 years .. 100 years we have been sitting this same sitting .. 100 years we have been looking at the paper .. 100 years we have been incapable even of incapacity itself .. 100 years astray, even while we stand on every road fit for arriving .. yet we are astray .. lost like a child whose mother lost him in a crowded train station when the power suddenly went out .. when people jostled and everything collided with everything .. The wicked raised him, and he drank of all their treachery and learned from all ...""")

t(74, 1915, """It is not justice that the neighbour in the south should go on pulling the cart like this forever! The difference is enormous, and the one being pulled along is determined to remain pulled along, and determined that the north remain pampered and rich and the south poor, lost and astray! The matter has dragged on .. the matter has become too absurd to be borne any longer!""")

